# DTF tier manifest: mcp-introspection-integrity
#   (artifact-keeper 1.12.0 introspection completion fixes:
#    #5461, #5462, #5464, #5466)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. No worker container: the oracle is the
# introspection worker. It mints an `mcp:introspect` API token for a service
# account and drives the Worker API (POST /api/v1/mcp/introspection/jobs/claim
# and /jobs/{id}/complete) with curl, so the remotes[] URL it publishes
# (https://mcp.example.invalid/mcp) is never contacted. Every outcome is read
# back through GET /mcp/{repo}/v0.1/servers/{name}/versions/{v}/capabilities.
# psql in the DB container (run.sh's DB_CONTAINER) is used for two things
# only: moving a claim's lease_expires_at into the past (#5462) and holding
# the job row FOR NO KEY UPDATE for a few seconds so concurrent completions
# queue on it deterministically, as the backend's own regression test does
# (#5461).
#
# RED images (two, both main):
#   sha-ad20810 (2026-11-06): predates #5530 (f811c6d1, #5462 and #5464) and
#     #5540 (9c1c8b76, #5466). It already carries #5433, whose transactional
#     claim lock closed the #5461 race, so FIX #5461 passes there.
#   sha-a837f88 (2026-11-05): the parent of #5433 (431521b2), the change that
#     actually fixed #5461 (#5530 only added the regression test, see its PR
#     body). Every FIX case fails there.
#   Ancestry checked with git merge-base --is-ancestor. 1.11.13 has no MCP
#   Registry at all.
# GREEN: main carrying all fix PRs (sha-2bdf092 or later).
#
# CONTROLS (pass on every image)
#   a live claim's ok result with valid metadata (ttlMs 2592000000,
#   cacheScope public) is stored and becomes current, and a sequential replay
#   of the same claim answers 409 mcp_claim_invalid and stores nothing; a
#   timeout result on attempt 1 answers retry and the job goes back to
#   pending with no snapshot; a fresher observation (ttlMs 0, cacheScope
#   private) replaces an older current one.
#
# FIX CASES
#   #5461 four concurrent divergent completions of one claim: exactly one
#     answers 200 stored, the others 409 mcp_claim_invalid, one snapshot is
#     stored; a retry racing an ok result of one claim has one winner and
#     never leaves a snapshot behind a pending job. Red (a837f88): all four
#     answer stored and four snapshots exist; the retry and the ok result
#     both answer 200 and the job is pending with a snapshot.
#   #5462 a claim whose lease has expired (the reaper has not run) answers
#     409 mcp_claim_invalid and stores nothing. Red: 200 stored, current.
#   #5464 a later-arriving result observed 3 minutes before the current
#     snapshot is kept as history and does not become current; an observedAt
#     an hour before the claim answers 400. Red: the stale result becomes
#     current; the pre-claim observedAt is stored.
#   #5466 ttlMs -1, cacheScope "shared" and an observedAt an hour ahead each
#     answer 400 mcp_invalid_result_metadata naming the field, store nothing
#     and leave the claim live (a corrected result is then stored). Red: 200
#     stored.
#
# NOT COVERED HERE: #5450, #5451 and #5636 are fixes in the
# ak-mcp-introspector binary, which no published image ships (see the PR).
#
# None of these issues has a security advisory (checked
# gh api repos/artifact-keeper/artifact-keeper/security-advisories), and the
# issues are public, so the tier asserts the full behaviour.
COVERS="5461 5462 5464 5466"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
